---
// The landing page at / (owner, 19 Nov): what designme.dev is, shown with the components themselves. The library it leads to is
// at /library (tools/site builds it as library.html). A full-width page with the site's header and footer and no sidebar.
// Sections, in order (owner, 19 Nov, after AlignUI, BoardUI and AffectUI: "I told you what to change from the references"):
//   hero      centred: the title, one short line, Browse the library and Read the docs
//   bento     right under it, on the page itself: twelve of the most distinctive components playing live, each its own card
//             in one of three stacks (two from 1100px, one below). Each card keeps the room its component takes at its tallest
//             (tools/site/bento-heights.json), and the component grows and shrinks in the middle of it, so no card moves the
//             cards under it as it plays; the stacks' cards share out what the tallest stack has over theirs, so the stacks end
//             level
//   screens   the two templates, whole apps made of the components, live in one frame on the site's grey, with a switch
//   wall      every component, as rows of pictures that drift in turn left and right across the site's grey, fading out at
//             both sides, each linking to its page, with Browse the library and GitHub
//   styles    Light or Dark, then Blueprint, Soft and Clean as a switch with the picked one's line and its <html> under it,
//             beside a demo on the site's grey; a pick restyles the whole page, and the control picked stays where it was
//   install   the CLI in HTML, React or Astro and the shadcn CLI, then an editor of what it writes: each file, its first
//             lines as installed (read from the registry) and the component they make, live; then a prompt for a coding agent
//   faq       questions, with their answers: the heading on the left, kept in view, and the list on the right
//   work      DesignMe's Book a call, the page's last word
// Section headings are large and centred, with one grey line under them: the landing page's exception to the 14px type rule
// (owner, 19 Nov, .claude/CLAUDE.md). /?headings=small shows them at 14px, to compare.
// No gradients (owner, 20 Nov: "lets go the minimal way"): the page is white, with the site's grey behind the templates, the
// wall and the styles demo. Shadows stay the neutral --dm-shadow and --dm-shadow-pop.
// Every number and claim here is read from the code or true of it: the counts come from the library's own sections, the
// file names, lengths and lines from the registry (/r), the facts from the README, the CLI and the docs. The demos are the
// installed HTML, CSS and JS on the shared core, as on a component page: they load from the registry (/r/<name>.json) when
// they come near the screen, and each stage fits the tallest its component gets in the style on screen
// (tools/site/card-heights.json), so nothing below it moves while it plays and no stage keeps room for another style.
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { ROOT, SITE, COMPONENTS, SECTIONS, SPLIT, BANDS, icon, MARKS, shadcnUrl } from '../lib/data.mjs';
import { FRAME_CSS, FRAME_JS } from '../lib/templates.mjs';

const comp = reg => { const c = COMPONENTS.find(x => x.reg === reg); if (!c) throw new Error('landing: no component called ' + reg); return c; };
const total = COMPONENTS.length;
const nOf = g => SECTIONS.filter(s => s.grp === g).reduce((n, s) => n + s.cards.length, 0);
const nAgent = nOf('agent'), nBasics = nOf('basics');

// each stage is as tall as its component gets in the style on screen (measure-heights.js measures each style: components is
// Soft), with its padding above and below, so the component sits in the middle and nothing below the stage moves while it
// plays. Picking another style fits the stages to it. Where a stage gives its component its whole width (440px, or 720px for
// a wide one), the tallest it gets is what the library measured at 1440px (band a); where it may give less, between 641 and
// 1099px, the most the library measured where its cards were at least as wide (band a, then c to i: b is the library's tight
// two-up band). On a phone the stages are as wide as the library's, so each band is its own
const MEASURED = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, 'tools/site/card-heights.json'), 'utf8'));
const KEYS = { soft:'components', bp:'componentsBp', clean:'componentsClean' }, PAD = 48;
const ROOMY = BANDS.map(([b, w], i) => ({ b, w, i })).filter(x => x.w > 640 && x.b !== 'b'), PHONE = BANDS.map(([b, w], i) => ({ b, w, i })).filter(x => x.w <= 640);
const heights = (c, style) => {
  const r = (MEASURED[KEYS[style]] || {})[c.v2], soft = MEASURED.components[c.v2];
  if (!soft) throw new Error('landing: no measured height for ' + c.v2 + ': measure it with measure-heights.js');
  return r && r.length === BANDS.length ? r : soft;
};
// a component with a switch under it (its views or designs, in a .dm frame) keeps 40px more for the switch, as on its own page
// (the library shows that switch in the card's footer, so its measurement leaves it out)
const SW = c => /class="[^"]*(?<![\w-])dm(?![\w-])/.test(c.html.html) ? 40 : 0;
// and 4px to spare, for the pixel or two a component can reach past what was measured at another width in its band
// same: one height in every style (the styles demo, which a pick restyles under the pointer)
const stageVars = (c, pad = PAD, same = false) => Object.keys(KEYS).flatMap(st => { const r = same ? BANDS.map((x, i) => Math.max(...Object.keys(KEYS).map(k => heights(c, k)[i]))) : heights(c, st), add = 2 * pad + SW(c) + 4;
  return [`--lh-${st}:${Math.max(...ROOMY.map(x => r[x.i])) + add}px`, ...PHONE.map(x => `--lh-${st}-${x.b}:${r[x.i] + add}px`)]; }).join(';');
// Blueprint draws when <html> has no data-style; each phone band applies from its own width up to the next one's
const pick = sfx => `.lp-demo{--lh:var(--lh-bp${sfx})}:root[data-style="soft"] .lp-demo{--lh:var(--lh-soft${sfx})}:root[data-style="clean"] .lp-demo{--lh:var(--lh-clean${sfx})}`;
const bandCss = [pick(''), ...PHONE.map((x, k) => `@media (max-width:${(k ? PHONE[k - 1].w : 641) - 1}px){${pick('-' + x.b)}}`), '.lp-demo{min-height:var(--lh)}'].join('\n');
// the bento's cards: each keeps the room its component takes at its tallest while it plays, at the card's own width in the
// style on screen (tools/site/measure-bento.js samples them on this page, each band at its narrowest width), with 4px to
// spare, and the component sits in the middle of it, so it grows and shrinks there and never moves the cards under it
// (a card it was pushing down by up to 236px as it played). A band applies from its own width up to the one before it
const BENTO_H = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, 'tools/site/bento-heights.json'), 'utf8'));
const bentoVars = c => Object.keys(KEYS).flatMap(st => { const r = (BENTO_H[st] || {})[c.reg];
  if (!r || r.length !== BENTO_H.bands.length) throw new Error(`landing: no bento height for ${c.reg} in ${st}: run tools/site/measure-bento.js`);
  return BENTO_H.bands.map(([b], i) => `--bh-${st}-${b}:${r[i] + 4}px`); }).join(';');
const pickB = b => `.lp-bc{--bh:var(--bh-bp-${b})}:root[data-style="soft"] .lp-bc{--bh:var(--bh-soft-${b})}:root[data-style="clean"] .lp-bc{--bh:var(--bh-clean-${b})}`;
const bentoCss = BENTO_H.bands.map(([b], i) => i ? `@media (max-width:${BENTO_H.bands[i - 1][1] - 1}px){${pickB(b)}}` : pickB(b)).join('\n');

// the bento: the library's most distinctive components, each its own card on the page (owner, 19 Nov: "the component is the
// tile"). No row of metric cards (owner, 19 Nov: "this is not some dashboard"); only components with a card of their own, so
// nothing sits loose on the page. Each card fills its stack's width and is as tall as it is right now, so the stacks are
// chosen to end close to level while every card plays (owner, 20 Nov: "do not leave spaces"): each candidate's height was
// sampled live for 110 seconds, every card in view, at a stack's width in each style, and these twelve, in these stacks,
// keep the stacks' feet within about 70px of each other for 90% of the time, also when the cards start at different
// moments. Agent tree (it grows by 260px over its run and starts again), Trace view (its detail lifts it by 390px for a few
// seconds), Eval results and Agent inbox (each empties for a moment as it starts again) are left out, and so is Top pages
// (its ranks are set in monospace). Three stacks from
// 1440px (the first wider, for Activity heatmap), two from 1100px (placed by the script under the bento), one below, in the
// three stacks' order. When a card here changes its height, sample them again and choose again.
// At launch only the live components are on the site (tools/site/live.js; owner, 24 Nov), so the bento is twelve live ones
// with a card of their own, and of those the steadiest: Context meter (it folds to a pill), Command palette, Composer, Model
// picker and Terminal stream change height by 110 to 340px as they play and are left out. Run cost sits in the first, wider
// stack, where its Raise cap button has room. Sampled for 60 seconds at 1440 with every card in view, the three stacks' feet
// were within about 45px of each other half of the time and 80px nine times in ten in Soft and Blueprint (their average
// bottoms within 25px), and about 70px and 113px in Clean, whose taller Knowledge sources and Scheduled runs lift the third stack.
// Knowledge sources, Plan review, Inline text diff, Agent lanes and Scheduled runs each still move by 35 to 90px as they play,
// so no choice of these twelve keeps the feet within 24px all the time. Since 26 Nov each card keeps the room its component
// takes at its tallest, with the component centred in it, and the stacks end level, so these moves stay inside their cards
// (run tools/site/measure-bento.js when a card here changes its height or a card is swapped)
const BENTO3 = [
  ['event-calendar', 'run-cost', 'run-drawer', 'agent-lanes'],
  ['tool-connections', 'memory-panel', 'plan-review', 'inline-text-diff'],
  ['agent-run-timeline', 'scheduled-runs', 'file-explorer', 'knowledge-sources'],
];
const BENTO2 = [
  ['event-calendar', 'knowledge-sources', 'run-drawer', 'tool-connections', 'run-cost', 'scheduled-runs'],
  ['memory-panel', 'agent-run-timeline', 'plan-review', 'file-explorer', 'agent-lanes', 'inline-text-diff'],
];
if ([...BENTO3.flat()].sort().join() !== [...BENTO2.flat()].sort().join()) throw new Error('landing: the bento\'s two layouts hold different cards');
const BENTO = BENTO3.map(stack => stack.map(comp));
// the templates' views, whole apps made of the components, each shown live in one frame on its own, without the app's sidebar
// (?embed=1&nav=0, and ?view= picks the view), so they read as the many views of one product (owner, 21 Nov: "show them, oh wow,
// there are so many different views"). A template's views share its frame: picking another one switches the view in the app
// already open. Another template's views join the list as they come (the Dashboard builder's will). The Workflow editor opens
// on its last test run (its own #run= address), so the run drawer under the canvas shows the run's steps and the screen is
// full, not a short flow on a tall empty canvas
const APPS = { 'sales-crm':'Sales CRM', 'workflow-editor':'Workflow editor', 'dashboard-builder':'Dashboard builder', 'whiteboard':'Whiteboard' };
const VIEWS = [['sales-crm', 'Accounts', 'accounts'], ['sales-crm', 'Pipeline', 'pipeline'], ['sales-crm', 'Calendar', 'calendar'],
  ['sales-crm', 'Forecast', 'forecast'], ['sales-crm', 'Reports', 'reports'], ['workflow-editor', 'Workflow', '', '#run=2087'],
  ['dashboard-builder', 'Dashboard', ''], ['whiteboard', 'Whiteboard', '']]
  .map(([slug, name, view, at = '']) => ({ slug, app:APPS[slug], name, view, at, url:`/templates/${slug}` }));
const openOf = v => v.url + (v.view ? `?view=${v.view}` : '');
// the wall: every component in the library, in its order, as four rows that drift in turn left and right
const ROWS = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(i => COMPONENTS.slice(Math.round(i * COMPONENTS.length / 4), Math.round((i + 1) * COMPONENTS.length / 4)));
if (ROWS.flat().length !== total) throw new Error('landing: the wall shows ' + ROWS.flat().length + ' of ' + total + ' components');
const STYLE_DEMO = comp('decision-prompt');
// the component the install commands and the editor name
const HERO = comp('permission-gate');

const STYLES = [
  ['bp', 'Blueprint', 'Square corners, hairline edges and a lime accent, like a technical sheet.', '<html>'],
  ['soft', 'Soft', 'Rounded, plush surfaces with a blue accent.', '<html data-style="soft">'],
  ['clean', 'Clean', 'Black, white and grey, with fully round controls. Data keeps its colours.', '<html data-style="clean">'],
];

// what `npx designme add <name>` writes, read from the registry the CLI reads (packages/designme/bin/designme.js): the
// component's own files, and the shared ones it adds once per project. React and Astro go into src/components/designme
// (components/designme in a project without src/), HTML into ./designme, the shadcn CLI into the components alias
const REG = p => JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, 'r', p + '.json'), 'utf8'));
const nLines = s => s.split('\n').length - (s.endsWith('\n') ? 1 : 0);
const plural = (n, w) => `${n} ${w}${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
// the first lines of a file, with a light tint: comments quieter, strings in the accent's text colour (no other colour)
const PREVIEW = 18;
const tint = (lines, ext) => {
  const blocks = /^(html|astro)$/.test(ext) ? [['<!--', '-->'], ['/*', '*/']] : [['/*', '*/']];
  const slash = /^(js|ts|tsx|astro)$/.test(ext);
  let end = null;
  return lines.map(l => {
    const out = []; let i = 0, plain = '';
    const flush = () => { if (plain){ out.push(['', plain]); plain = ''; } };
    while (i < l.length){
      if (end){ const j = l.indexOf(end, i), k = j < 0 ? l.length : j + end.length; flush(); out.push(['cm', l.slice(i, k)]); i = k; if (j >= 0) end = null; continue; }
      const b = blocks.find(([o]) => l.startsWith(o, i));
      if (b){ const j = l.indexOf(b[1], i + b[0].length), k = j < 0 ? l.length : j + b[1].length; if (j < 0) end = b[1]; flush(); out.push(['cm', l.slice(i, k)]); i = k; continue; }
      if (slash && l.startsWith('//', i) && l[i - 1] !== ':'){ flush(); out.push(['cm', l.slice(i)]); i = l.length; continue; }
      const q = l[i];
      if (q === '"' || q === "'" || q === '`'){ let j = i + 1; while (j < l.length && l[j] !== q){ if (l[j] === '\\') j++; j++; } if (j < l.length){ flush(); out.push(['st', l.slice(i, j + 1)]); i = j + 1; continue; } }
      plain += q; i++;
    }
    flush(); return out;
  });
};
const ext = p => (p.match(/\.(\w+)$/) || [, ''])[1];
const file = (p, f, depth) => { const n = nLines(f.content); return { path:p, name:p.slice(p.lastIndexOf('/') + 1), depth, n, meta:plural(n, 'line'), head:tint(f.content.split('\n').slice(0, Math.min(PREVIEW, n)), ext(p)) }; };
// a folder of shared helpers, as one row that lists what is in it
const folder = (files, dir, depth) => { const list = files.map(f => [f.path.slice(dir.length), nLines(f.content)]), w = Math.max(...list.map(x => x[0].length));
  return { path:dir, name:dir, depth, folder:true, n:files.length, meta:plural(files.length, 'file'), head:list.map(([f, n]) => [['', `${f.padEnd(w)}  `], ['cm', plural(n, 'line')]]) }; };
const strip = (files, pre) => files.map(f => ({ ...f, path:f.path.startsWith(pre) ? f.path.slice(pre.length) : f.path }));
const needs = (core, item) => { const f = core.files.filter(x => item.needs.includes(x.path)); if (f.length !== item.needs.length) throw new Error('landing: a shared file ' + HERO.reg + ' needs is missing from the registry'); return f; };
// a tab's tree: the root, the component's folder with its files, then what is shared (a folder of its own, or files at the
// root and a lib/ folder), each row with its depth
const tree = (root, own, shared) => {
  const rows = [{ dir:true, name:root, depth:0 }, { dir:true, name:`${HERO.reg}/`, depth:1 }, ...own.map(f => file(f.path, f, 2))];
  const sub = shared.filter(f => f.path.includes('/')), top = shared.filter(f => !f.path.includes('/'));
  const dirs = [...new Set(sub.map(f => f.path.slice(0, f.path.indexOf('/') + 1)))];
  top.forEach(f => rows.push({ ...file(f.path, f, 1), once:true }));
  dirs.forEach(d => { const in_ = sub.filter(f => f.path.startsWith(d));
    if (d === 'lib/') rows.push({ ...folder(in_, d, 1), once:true });
    else { rows.push({ dir:true, name:d, depth:1, once:true }); in_.forEach(f => rows.push(file(f.path, f, 2))); } });
  return rows;
};
const FILES = (() => {
  const h = REG(HERO.reg), r = REG('react/' + HERO.reg), a = REG('astro/' + HERO.reg), s = REG('shadcn/' + HERO.reg);
  const demo = { path:`${HERO.reg}/demo.html`, name:'demo.html', depth:2, meta:'written by the CLI', demo:true };
  const html = tree('designme/', h.files, REG('core').files); html.splice(2 + h.files.length, 0, demo);
  return {
    html:{ root:'designme/', rows:html },
    react:{ root:'src/components/designme/', rows:tree('src/components/designme/', r.files, needs(REG('react/core'), r)) },
    astro:{ root:'src/components/designme/', rows:tree('src/components/designme/', a.files, needs(REG('astro/core'), a)) },
    shadcn:{ root:'components/designme/', alias:true, rows:tree('designme/', strip(s.files, 'designme/'), strip(REG('shadcn/core').files, 'designme/')) },
  };
})();

const INSTALL = [
  ['html', 'HTML', MARKS.html, `npx designme add ${HERO.reg}`, 'Open demo.html to see it working, then copy its markup into your page.'],
  ['react', 'React', MARKS.react, `npx designme add ${HERO.reg} --react`, 'A typed component that brings its own CSS, for React 19 and up.'],
  ['astro', 'Astro', MARKS.astro, `npx designme add ${HERO.reg} --astro`, 'The same markup, CSS and script as the HTML one, as an .astro component.'],
  ['shadcn', 'shadcn', MARKS.react, `npx shadcn@latest add ${shadcnUrl(HERO.reg)}`, 'Every component is also a shadcn registry item, in React or in Astro.'],
];

const FAQ = [
  ['Is it free?', 'Yes. Every component is free for personal and commercial work under the MIT licence. Fonts, icons, flags and brand marks from other projects keep their own licences, listed in NOTICE.md.'],
  ['What do I need?', 'Node 18 or later to run the CLI. The React components need React 19 and work in Next.js, Vite and Astro islands. The HTML version needs only the shared core, which the CLI adds once.'],
  ['Do I need Tailwind or shadcn/ui?', 'No. The components bring their own CSS. If your project uses shadcn/ui or Tailwind v4, the theme bridge (--theme-bridge) gives them your theme, and the shadcn CLI can add any of them.'],
  ['Will their CSS clash with mine?', 'No. Every CSS variable starts with --dm-, and in React every class and animation name starts with dm- too, so nothing meets your own names.'],
  ['Are they accessible?', 'They come with ARIA roles and labels, live regions for what the agent is doing, keyboard support in most components, tap areas on touch screens, and reduced motion.'],
  ['What are Blueprint, Soft and Clean?', 'Three styles for the same components: Blueprint is technical and square with a lime accent, Soft is rounded with a blue accent, and Clean is black, white and grey with fully round controls. Each has a light and a dark theme. In your project, data-style on <html> picks one.'],
  ['Can AI coding tools use it?', 'Yes. Every component and docs page has a Markdown copy at its address plus .md, and llms.txt lists every component with its install command. The Using with AI page in the docs has prompts to start from.'],
  ['Is there a Figma file?', 'It is in progress on the roadmap. Leave your email in the library and you will get it when it lands.'],
  ['Who made it?', 'DesignMe, a design and development studio working with startups and enterprises. If you want help building your product, book a call.'],
];

// the prompt the docs give a coding agent (Using with AI), for any screen
const PROMPT = `Read ${SITE}/llms.txt and pick the components for our screen.\nFor each one, read its .md page, then install it with:\n  npx designme add <name> --react\nKeep the installed files as they are and drive the components through their props from our state.`;
const BOOK = 'https://www.designme.agency/intro?utm_source=designme.dev&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=book_a_call';
const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/bydesignme/designme-dev';
const GH_MARK = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385.6.113.82-.258.82-.577 0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729 1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236 1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93 0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176 0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405 1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405 2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22 0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92.42.36.81 1.096.81 2.22 0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286 0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12"/></svg>';
const replayIcon = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7L3 8"/><path d="M3 3v5h5"/></svg>';
const folderIcon = '<svg class="lp-fi" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.25 4.75c0-.83.67-1.5 1.5-1.5h2.4c.4 0 .78.16 1.06.44l.85.81h4.19c.83 0 1.5.67 1.5 1.5v5.25c0 .83-.67 1.5-1.5 1.5h-8.5c-.83 0-1.5-.67-1.5-1.5z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>';
const arrow = icon('arrow_forward', 'lp-ar');
const fileIcon = icon('description', 'lp-fi');
// a command in words that each stay whole, so on a phone it wraps at a space (an address may also wrap after a slash)
const words = cmd => cmd.split(' ').map(w => /^https?:/.test(w) ? w.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/\//g, '/<wbr>') : `<span class="lp-w">${w.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;')}</span>`).join(' ');
// `code` in the copy becomes <code>
const md = s => s.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;').replace(/(--[\w-]+|&lt;html&gt;|NOTICE\.md|\.md\b|llms\.txt|data-style)/g, '<code>$1</code>');

const title = 'Designme.dev: free UI components for AI agent products';
const description = `${total} free, MIT-licensed UI components for products built around AI agents, in HTML, React or Astro, in three styles with light and dark mode.`;
const jsonld = [
  { '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'WebSite', name:'Designme.dev', url:SITE + '/', description,
    publisher:{ '@type':'Organization', name:'DesignMe', url:'https://designme.agency' } },
  { '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity:FAQ.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type':'Question', name:q, acceptedAnswer:{ '@type':'Answer', text:a } })) },
];
---
<Page title={title} description={description} path="/" jsonld={jsonld}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script is:inline>
    // the section headings at 14px, as the type rule sets text everywhere else, to compare with the large ones: /?headings=small
    if (/[?&]headings=small(&|$)/.test(location.search)) document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-lp-h', 'small');
    // the library used to be here: its old addresses (/#/changelog, /#s-status, /#/agent-tree, /?q=…) open it at /library
    (function(){ var h = location.hash, q = /[?&]q=/.test(location.search); if (q || /^#(\/|s-|c-|components$)/.test(h)) location.replace('/library' + location.search + h); })();
    </script>
    <script async src="https://plausible.io/js/pa-0ymYxWA7A4pvtqpGbOCwQ.js"></script>
    <script is:inline>window.plausible=window.plausible||function(){(plausible.q=plausible.q||[]).push(arguments)},plausible.init=plausible.init||function(i){plausible.o=i||{}};plausible.init()</script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/components/assets/core.css">
    <style is:inline set:html={FRAME_CSS} />
    <style is:inline set:html={bandCss} />
    <style is:inline set:html={bentoCss} />
    <style is:global>
      .pg-main:has(.lp){padding:0}
      /* the page keeps what the reader sees still by itself (the script at the end), the same in every browser, so the
         browser's own scroll anchoring is off here */
      html:has(.lp),html:has(.lp) body{overflow-anchor:none}
      /* and the page scrolls at once when asked to (the landing page has no in-page links to glide to): a glide in progress
         would be cut short each time the page makes up for a block above the view */
      html:has(.lp){scroll-behavior:auto}
      /* one rhythm for the whole page: sections 160px apart (120px on a tablet, 96px on a phone), everything else on the 4px
         scale; one family of corners (r1 for fields and rows, r2 for tiles, windows and frames, r3 for backdrops): Soft's
         plush and squircled, Clean's a little rounder and never squircled, and Blueprint keeps the site's rounded page
         around its square components, as on a component page; one easing, Clean's */
      .lp{--lp-sec:160px;--lp-ease:cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1);--lp-r1:10px;--lp-r2:16px;--lp-r3:28px;--lp-hair:color-mix(in srgb,var(--pg-line2) 50%,transparent)}
      :root[data-style="clean"] .lp{--lp-r2:22px;--lp-r3:30px}
      @supports (corner-shape:squircle){
        :root[data-style="soft"] .lp{--lp-r1:16px;--lp-r2:26px;--lp-r3:44px}
        :root[data-style="soft"] :is(.lp-bg,.lp-win,.lp-show,.lp-show .dvf-dev:not(.mobile),.lp-wt,.lp-wt img,.lp-line,.lp-prompt pre){corner-shape:squircle}
      }
      .lp-in{max-width:1464px;margin:0 auto;padding-inline:32px}
      .lp code{font:500 12.5px/1.4 var(--pg-mono);font-variant-ligatures:none;background:var(--pg-chip);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:5px;color:var(--pg-fg)}
      .lp-ar{display:block;width:14px;height:14px;flex:none}

      /* ---- hero: centred, the words and the two buttons ---- */
      .lp-hero{padding-top:120px;text-align:center}
      /* the page's title: the page-title exception to the type rule (.pg-h1) */
      .pg-h1.lp-h1{max-width:920px;margin:0 auto;font-size:clamp(36px,4.4vw,64px);line-height:1.04;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.04em;text-wrap:balance}
      .lp-lead{margin:24px auto 0;max-width:640px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--pg-dim);text-wrap:balance}
      .lp-cta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:32px}
      .lp-hero .lp-cta{justify-content:center}
      /* buttons: the components' own (.pill, .pill.primary on the accent, .pill.line), a step taller on the page */
      .lp .lp-btn{height:40px;padding:0 18px;font-size:14px;text-decoration:none;gap:8px}
      .lp .lp-btn svg{width:14px;height:14px}

      /* ---- section headings: large and centred, one grey line under them (the landing page's exception to the 14px
         type rule, owner 19 Nov). /?headings=small sets them at 14px, on the left of the column, to compare ---- */
      .lp-sec{padding-top:var(--lp-sec)}
      .lp-sh{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:16px;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto 56px;text-align:center}
      .lp-sh h2{margin:0;font-size:clamp(30px,3.2vw,44px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.032em;text-wrap:balance;color:var(--pg-fg)}
      .lp-sh p{margin:0;max-width:540px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--pg-dim);text-wrap:balance}
      .lp-sh .lp-more{margin-top:4px}
      :root[data-lp-h="small"] .lp-sh{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,5fr) minmax(0,7fr);align-items:start;gap:8px 48px;max-width:none;margin:0 0 48px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--pg-line);text-align:left}
      :root[data-lp-h="small"] .lp-sh h2{font-size:14px;line-height:20px;letter-spacing:0}
      :root[data-lp-h="small"] .lp-sh p{grid-column:2;text-wrap:wrap}
      :root[data-lp-h="small"] .lp-sh .lp-more{grid-column:2;justify-self:start;margin-top:0}
      @media (max-width:860px){:root[data-lp-h="small"] .lp-sh{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}:root[data-lp-h="small"] .lp-sh :is(p,.lp-more){grid-column:1}}
      .lp-more{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:var(--pg-fg);text-decoration:none}
      .lp-more:hover .lp-ar{transform:translateX(2px)}
      .lp-more .lp-ar{transition:transform 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      /* a smaller block inside a section: its heading and what it is on the left, its content on the right */
      .lp-two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,5fr) minmax(0,7fr);gap:24px 48px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--pg-line)}
      .lp-h h3{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:20px;font-weight:500;color:var(--pg-fg)}
      .lp-h p{margin:8px 0 0;max-width:52ch;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--pg-dim)}
      .lp-h .lp-more{margin-top:16px}
      .lp-h p a{color:var(--pg-fg)}
      @media (max-width:860px){.lp-two{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}

      /* ---- a demo's stage: the component in the middle of the site's grey, as on a component page ---- */
      .lp-demo{flex:1;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);justify-items:center;align-items:center;padding:48px 24px;overflow-anchor:none}
      /* a picked style fits each stage to it; the visitor's own click, so the page may move then */
      .lp-demo>.card{min-width:0;align-self:stretch;display:grid;place-items:center}
      .lp-miss{margin:0;color:var(--pg-dim);font-size:14px}
            .lp-anim{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:6px;height:28px;padding:0 12px;border:0;border-radius:999px;background:var(--pg-bg);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--pg-line2);color:var(--pg-dim);font:500 13px/1 var(--pg-sans);cursor:pointer;transition:color 220ms var(--lp-ease),background-color 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-anim:hover{color:var(--pg-fg);background:var(--pg-soft)}
      .lp-anim svg{width:14px;height:14px}

      /* ---- the bento: each component its own card, straight on the page, in stacks. A card's place keeps the room its
         component takes at its tallest (--bh, from bento-heights.json, also while it loads), and the component grows and
         shrinks in the middle of it, so no card moves the cards under it. The stacks are as tall as the tallest, and each
         stack's cards share out the difference, so the stacks end level ---- */
      .lp .lp-bento-w{margin-top:80px;padding:0 32px}
      .lp-bento{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:24px;max-width:1376px;margin:0 auto;align-items:stretch}
      .lp-stack{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px;min-width:0}
      .lp-bt{min-width:0;flex:1 0 auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
      .lp .lp-bt .lp-bc{flex:1 0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);align-items:center;min-height:var(--bh,320px);padding:0}
      .lp .lp-bt .lp-bc>.card{display:block;width:100%;max-width:none;align-self:center}
      /* the card fills its stack: its own widest size (a max-width the component keeps for a stage) gives way here */
      .lp-bt .stage-in,.lp-bt .stage-in>*{max-width:none}
      @media (min-width:641px) and (max-width:1099px){.lp-bt{width:100%;max-width:720px;margin-inline:auto}}
      .lp-stack:empty{display:none}
      @media (min-width:1100px){
        .lp-bento{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(0,1fr)}
        .lp-stack:nth-child(3){grid-column:2}
      }
      @media (min-width:1440px){
        .lp-bento{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr)}
        .lp-stack:nth-child(3){grid-column:auto}
      }

      /* ---- screens: the templates' views, live in one frame on the site's grey, with the switch between them over it. On a
         phone the switch's row scrolls sideways (the picked view kept in sight) ---- */
      .lp-show-bar{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;align-items:center;gap:16px;margin-bottom:24px}
      .lp-tabs{grid-column:2;min-width:0}
      .lp-show-bar .pg-seg button{flex:none;height:32px;padding:0 14px;white-space:nowrap}
      .lp-open{grid-column:3;justify-self:end}
      .lp-open .lp-ar{transform:rotate(-45deg)}
      .lp-more.lp-open:hover .lp-ar{transform:rotate(-45deg) translateX(2px)}
      /* the frame keeps its size from the start (the app inside fades in once it has loaded) and whatever the view: the app at
         the frame's width, 800px tall, scaled down below 1280px wide; on a phone, the app's phone layout in a phone's frame */
      .lp-show{--dvf-line:var(--pg-line2);--dvf-bg:var(--pg-bg);width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;max-height:800px;border-radius:var(--lp-r2);background:var(--pg-bg);box-shadow:var(--dm-shadow-pop)}
      .lp-show .dvf-dev:not(.mobile){border-radius:var(--lp-r2)}
      .lp-show-ph{position:absolute;inset:0;display:grid;place-items:center;margin:0;color:var(--pg-dim);font-size:13px}

      /* ---- the site's grey behind the templates and the styles demo, as a component's stage has it ---- */
      .lp-bg{position:relative;padding:56px;border-radius:var(--lp-r3);background:var(--pg-soft)}
      :root[data-style="clean"] .lp-bg{background:var(--dm-stage)}

      /* ---- a window: a title bar, then what is in it ---- */
      .lp-win{position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;border-radius:var(--lp-r2);background:var(--pg-bg);box-shadow:var(--dm-shadow-pop);overflow:hidden}
      .lp-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;min-height:44px;padding:8px 8px 8px 16px;box-shadow:inset 0 -1px 0 var(--lp-hair);font-size:13px;line-height:20px;color:var(--pg-muted)}
      :root[data-style="clean"] .lp-bar{background:var(--dm-strip)}
      .lp-bar-l{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:0 8px;min-width:0}
      .lp-bar a{color:var(--pg-dim);font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;transition:color 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-bar a:hover{color:var(--pg-fg)}
      .lp-bar a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--pg-focus);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:4px}
      .lp-panes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);background:var(--pg-soft)}
      :root[data-style="clean"] .lp-panes{background:var(--dm-stage)}
      .lp-pane{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}

      /* ---- the wall: every component, four rows that drift in turn left and right across the site's grey the full width of
         the window, fading out into the grey at both sides. A row holds still under the pointer or while a tile in it has the
         focus; with reduced motion the rows stand still and scroll by hand ---- */
      .lp .lp-rows{--lp-wg:var(--pg-soft);position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;padding:56px 0;background:var(--lp-wg)}
      :root[data-style="clean"] .lp .lp-rows{--lp-wg:var(--dm-stage)}
      .lp-rows::before,.lp-rows::after{content:"";position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;z-index:2;width:min(160px,12vw);pointer-events:none}
      .lp-rows::before{left:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--lp-wg),transparent)}
      .lp-rows::after{right:0;background:linear-gradient(270deg,var(--lp-wg),transparent)}
      /* each row clips the tiles that drift past its ends, with room above and below for their shadows */
      .lp-row{overflow:hidden;padding:16px 0;margin:-16px 0}
      .lp-track{display:flex;width:max-content;animation:lp-drift var(--dur,200s) linear infinite}
      .lp-row.rev .lp-track{animation-direction:reverse}
      .lp-set{display:flex;gap:16px;padding-right:16px}
      @keyframes lp-drift{to{transform:translateX(-50%)}}
      .lp-row:hover .lp-track,.lp-row:focus-within .lp-track{animation-play-state:paused}
      .lp-wt{flex:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;width:240px;padding:6px 6px 10px;border-radius:var(--lp-r2);background:var(--pg-bg);box-shadow:var(--dm-shadow);color:var(--pg-fg);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-wt:hover{background:var(--pg-soft)}
      .lp-wt:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--pg-focus);outline-offset:-2px}
      .lp-wt img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:16/10;border-radius:max(0px,calc(var(--lp-r2) - 6px));background:var(--pg-soft)}
      .lp-wt span{padding:0 4px;font-size:13px;line-height:18px;font-weight:500;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
      @media (max-width:640px){.lp-wt{width:176px}.lp .lp-rows{padding:24px 0;margin:0}}
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.lp-track{animation:none}.lp-set[aria-hidden]{display:none}.lp-row{overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none}.lp-row::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}}

      /* ---- styles: Light or Dark, then the three styles, each a switch of the site's own (.pg-seg), with the picked style's
         line and its attribute under them; beside them the demo, alone on the site's grey ---- */
      .lp-sty{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,5fr) minmax(0,7fr);gap:32px 48px;align-items:start}
      .lp-pick{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:20px}
      .lp-pk{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:8px}
      .lp-pkl{font-size:13px;line-height:20px;color:var(--pg-muted)}
      .lp .lp-seg button{height:32px;padding:0 16px;font-size:14px}
      /* the three styles' lines share one place, as tall as the longest, so a pick never moves what is under it */
      .lp-sds{display:grid}
      .lp-sd{grid-area:1/1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px;max-width:44ch}
      .lp-sd[hidden]{display:flex;visibility:hidden}
      .lp-sd p{margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--pg-dim)}
      .lp-sd code{font-size:12px}
      .lp-stg{padding:0;overflow:hidden}
      .lp-stg .lp-rp{position:absolute;top:12px;right:12px;z-index:3;width:28px;padding:0;opacity:0;transition:opacity 220ms var(--lp-ease),color 220ms var(--lp-ease),background-color 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-stg:hover .lp-rp,.lp-stg:focus-within .lp-rp{opacity:1}
      @media (hover:none){.lp-stg .lp-rp{opacity:1}}
      @media (max-width:1099px){.lp-sty{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}}

      /* ---- install: the command for each way to add it, centred, then the editor of what it writes ---- */
      .lp-add{min-width:0}
      .lp-cmd{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto}
      .lp-tl{display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:4px;margin:0 0 16px;overflow-x:auto;scrollbar-width:none;box-shadow:inset 0 -1px 0 var(--pg-line)}
      @media (pointer:coarse){.lp-tl{padding:2px 0;margin:-2px 0 14px;box-shadow:none;background:linear-gradient(var(--pg-line),var(--pg-line)) 0 calc(100% - 2px)/100% 1px no-repeat}}
      .lp-tl button{position:relative;flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;height:40px;padding:0 12px;border:0;background:none;color:var(--pg-dim);font:400 14px/1 var(--pg-sans);cursor:pointer;transition:color 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-tl button:hover,.lp-tl button[aria-selected="true"]{color:var(--pg-fg)}
      .lp-tl button::after{content:"";position:absolute;left:12px;right:12px;bottom:0;height:2px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--pg-fg);transform:scaleX(0);transition:transform 340ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-tl button[aria-selected="true"]::after{transform:scaleX(1)}
      .lp-tl .cp-mk{width:16px;height:16px}
      .lp-line{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-width:0;min-height:48px;padding:8px 8px 8px 16px;border-radius:var(--lp-r1);background:var(--pg-soft);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--pg-line)}
      .lp .lp-line code{background:none;padding:0;border-radius:0;color:var(--pg-fg)}
      .lp .lp-line .d{flex:none;color:var(--pg-muted);font:500 13px/1 var(--pg-mono)}
      .lp .lp-line .c{flex:1;min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:500 13px/1.5 var(--pg-mono)}
      .lp-line .lp-w{white-space:nowrap}
      .lp-copy{flex:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:28px;padding:0 12px;border:0;border-radius:999px;background:var(--pg-bg);color:var(--pg-fg);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--pg-line2);font:500 13px/1 var(--pg-sans);cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      .lp-copy:hover{background:var(--pg-chip)}
      .lp-copy svg{width:14px;height:14px}
      .lp-tp>p{margin:16px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--pg-dim);text-wrap:balance}
      /* the editor: the files on the left as a tree (the component's own, then the shared ones it adds once per project),
         the first lines of the one picked in the middle, and the component they make on the right, live */
      .lp-ed-art{margin-top:48px}
      .lp-ed-art .lp-win{max-width:1216px}
      .lp-ed .lp-bar{justify-content:flex-start}
      .lp .lp-ed .lp-bar code{font-size:12px}
      .lp-ed-b{display:grid;grid-template-columns:248px minmax(0,1fr);grid-template-areas:"tree code" "pv pv"}
      @media (min-width:1100px){.lp-ed-b{grid-template-columns:248px minmax(0,1fr) 488px;grid-template-areas:"tree code pv"}}
      .lp-ed-f{display:contents}
      .lp-ed-f[hidden]{display:none}
      .lp-tree{grid-area:tree;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;min-width:0;padding:12px 8px;box-shadow:inset -1px 0 0 var(--lp-hair)}
      .lp-tr{position:relative;display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px minmax(0,1fr) auto;align-items:center;gap:8px;width:100%;height:30px;padding:0 8px 0 calc(8px + var(--d,0) * 16px);border:0;border-radius:var(--lp-r1);background:none;color:var(--pg-dim);font:400 13px/1 var(--pg-sans);text-align:left}
      /* an indent guide under each folder, down the side of what is in it */
      .lp-tr:is([style*="--d:1"],[style*="--d:2"])::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:15px;top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:var(--lp-hair)}
      .lp-tr[style*="--d:2"]::before{left:31px;box-shadow:-16px 0 0 var(--lp-hair)}
      .lp-tr.dir{color:var(--pg-fg)}
      button.lp-tr{cursor:pointer;transition:background-color 220ms var(--lp-ease),color 220ms var(--lp-ease),box-shadow 220ms var(--lp-ease)}
      button.lp-tr:hover{background:var(--pg-soft);color:var(--pg-fg)}
      button.lp-tr[aria-selected="true"]{background:var(--pg-bg);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--pg-line2);color:var(--pg-fg)}
      button.lp-tr:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--pg-focus);outline-offset:-2px}
      .lp-tr .n{min-width:0;line-height:20px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
      .lp-tr .m{font-size:12px;color:var(--pg-muted);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
      .lp-fi{width:16px;height:16px;color:var(--pg-muted)}
      .lp-code{grid-area:code;min-width:0;min-height:360px;position:relative}
      .lp-cp{position:absolute;inset:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
      .lp-cp[hidden]{display:none}
      .lp-cph{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;min-height:44px;margin:0;padding:12px 16px;box-shadow:inset 0 -1px 0 var(--lp-hair);font-size:12px;line-height:20px;color:var(--pg-muted)}
      .lp .lp-cph code{min-width:0;background:none;padding:0;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;color:var(--pg-fg);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
      .lp-cph span{flex:none}
      .lp-cp pre{flex:1;min-height:0;margin:0;padding:12px 16px 16px 0;overflow:auto;font:500 12px/20px var(--pg-mono);font-variant-ligatures:none;color:var(--pg-fg);counter-reset:ln;scrollbar-width:thin}
      .lp .lp-cp pre code{display:block;width:max-content;min-width:100%;background:none;padding:0;border-radius:0;font:inherit;color:inherit}
      .lp-cp pre .l{display:block;white-space:pre;counter-increment:ln}
      .lp-cp pre .l::before{content:counter(ln);display:inline-block;width:32px;margin-right:16px;text-align:right;color:var(--pg-muted);user-select:none}
      .lp-cp pre .cm{color:var(--pg-muted)}
      .lp-cp pre .st{color:var(--dm-accent-fg,var(--pg-fg))}
      .lp-cp pre.ls{padding-left:16px}
      .lp-cp pre.ls .l::before{content:none}
      /* a file longer than what is shown fades out at the foot */
      .lp-cp pre.cut{-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(#000 calc(100% - 72px),transparent);mask-image:linear-gradient(#000 calc(100% - 72px),transparent)}
      .lp-cp pre:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--pg-focus);outline-offset:-2px}
      .lp-cpn{margin:0;padding:16px;max-width:52ch;font-size:13px;line-height:20px;color:var(--pg-dim)}
      .lp-pv{grid-area:pv;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;background:var(--pg-soft);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 var(--lp-hair)}
      @media (min-width:1100px){.lp-pv{box-shadow:inset 1px 0 0 var(--lp-hair)}}
      :root[data-style="clean"] .lp-pv{background:var(--dm-stage)}
      .lp-pvh{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px;min-height:44px;padding:8px 8px 8px 16px;box-shadow:inset 0 -1px 0 var(--lp-hair);font-size:12px;line-height:20px;color:var(--pg-muted)}
